{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3007","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3007","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3007\",\"parent_revision\":\"89e8899b338d1001068f3457369eb964996dfcd89b86a874c3e0d409983e05e4\",\"root_revision\":\"89e8899b338d1001068f3457369eb964996dfcd89b86a874c3e0d409983e05e4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n67 of 80 files under plugins/*/scripts/*.py and plugins/*/skills/*/scripts/*.py use the shebang `#!/usr/bin/env -S uv --quiet run --active --script`; only 5 use the documented-canonical `#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --quiet --script` (AGENTS.md Gotcha #12).\\n\\nEmpirically verified on uv 0.12.5: with VIRTUAL_ENV set to the repo .venv, `--active` causes `uv run --script` to install the PEP 723 script's inline dependencies into that active venv instead of an isolated ephemeral environment (confirmed via sys.executable and package install location; a falsification control without --active correctly used the ephemeral env). This defeats PEP 723 isolation and silently drifts .venv from uv.lock whenever any agent runs one of the 67 affected scripts from a shell with an activated venv.\\n\\nFix: rewrite all 67 shebangs to drop --active, canonicalizing on `uv run --quiet --script`.\\n\\nThis is a pre-existing bug that predates the astral migration. The migration's own A3 node documents the correct form going forward in .claude/rules/script-invocation.md but deliberately does not touch the 67 existing files (scoped out by user decision to avoid diff bloat in that branch) \u2014 tracked here instead.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **rewrite --active pep 723 shebangs (67 files) \u2014 silently pollutes shared .venv** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered during A2 audit of astral plugin migration (task-graph node A2)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5e865be50fd34b0caba4137e2b46e8d3b103190abe808f6e6da7d946e0893312\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiIh4g\"}"}